<title>USA: CROPS IN MISSISSIPPI RECEIVE NEEDED RAINS.</title>
<headline>CROPS IN MISSISSIPPI RECEIVE NEEDED RAINS.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the weekly crop update from the Mississippi Agricultural Statistics Service for the week ended Sunday August 10.</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>According to the Mississippi Agricultural Statistics Service, there were 2.5 days suitable for fieldwork for the week ending August 10, 1997. The main farming activities for the week were spraying for insects, weed control, and harvesting hay. Rain halted some farm activities, but it was much needed throughout the state. Soil moisture conditions  were rated 5 percent very short, 10 percent short, 46 percent adequate and 39 percent surplus.</p>
